  "summary": "An MLive weekend roundup leads with a brief note that Michigan gubernatorial candidates are staking out positions on Flock ALPR cameras: Republican John James frames it as balancing public safety and constitutional privacy, while Democrat Jocelyn Benson cites a lack of transparency as the main issue. The Flock item is one of five unrelated 'must-read' summaries.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Michigan gubernatorial candidates are beginning to define their positions on Flock cameras, automated license plate readers that have become increasingly controversial as their use expands across the state.",
